-### ProNeRF
-ProNeRF is a few-point volumetric rendering method that uses a Projection-Aware Sampling (PAS) network to predict sparse 3D sampling points and opacity adjustments, allowing high-quality rendering with significantly fewer samples than standard NeRF [S1, unofficial]. It achieves faster inference than vanilla NeRF with higher quality than HyperReel by combining a coarse-to-fine sampling strategy with an alternating exploration-exploitation training loop [S1, unofficial]. Unlike generalizable radiance fields that store all training input images for epipolar feature projection, ProNeRF uses a fixed subset of reference views, ensuring a consistent memory footprint [S1, unofficial].
