-### Deformable Radiance Fields
-Deformable Radiance Fields represent a dynamic surgical scene as a static canonical radiance field and a time-dependent displacement field to handle non-rigid deformations [S5]. Preprocessing maps input coordinates and time into Fourier features using positional encoding $\gamma(\cdot)$ before feeding to the networks. Color and occupancy at time $t$ for point $x$ are retrieved as $F_\Theta(x + G_\Phi(x, t), d)$ [S5]. The Canonical field $F_\Theta(x, d)$ is an 8-layer MLP with parameters $\Theta$. Inputs: coordinates $x \in \mathbb{R}^3$, unit view direction $d \in \mathbb{R}^3$. Outputs: RGB color $c(x, d) \in \mathbb{R}^3$, space occupancy $\sigma(x) \in \mathbb{R}$. The Displacement field $G_\Phi(x, t)$ is an 8-layer MLP with parameters $\Phi$. Inputs: space-time coordinates $(x, t)$. Output: displacement vector between point $x$ at time $t$ and corresponding point in canonical field [S5].
+#### Deformable Radiance Fields
+- [S5] Represents a dynamic surgical scene as a static canonical radiance field and a time-dependent displacement field to handle non-rigid deformations.
+- [S5] Preprocessing: Map input coordinates and time into Fourier features using positional encoding γ(·) before feeding to the networks.
+- [S5] Color and occupancy at time t for point x are retrieved as F_Θ(x + G_Φ(x, t), d).
+- [S5] Canonical field F_Θ(x, d): 8-layer MLP with parameters Θ. Inputs: coordinates x ∈ R^3, unit view direction d ∈ R^3. Outputs: RGB color c(x, d) ∈ R^3, space occupancy σ(x) ∈ R.
+- [S5] Displacement field G_Φ(x, t): 8-layer MLP with parameters Φ. Inputs: space-time coordinates (x, t). Output: displacement vector between point x at time t and corresponding point in canonical field.
